    <ferc:IncreasesDecreasesDueToMiscellaneousPaidInCapital id="f-954" contextRef="c-158" unitRef="u-3" decimals="0">-2700000</ferc:IncreasesDecreasesDueToMiscellaneousPaidInCapital>
    <ferc:OrderNumber id="f-955" contextRef="c-158" unitRef="u-01" decimals="0">1</ferc:OrderNumber>
    <ferc:OtherPaidInCapitalDescription id="f-956" contextRef="c-158">Account 11 Miscellaneous Paid-In Capital</ferc:OtherPaidInCapitalDescription>
    <ferc:AnnualFilingsContainingInputsToFormulaRates id="f-958" contextRef="c-51">true</ferc:AnnualFilingsContainingInputsToFormulaRates>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-960" contextRef="c-51">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 4.6pt; margin-left: 22.75pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.8pt; font-weight: bold; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;POLICIES&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold"&gt;Nature of Operations&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.25pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Citizens Sunrise Transmission, LLC (CST or the Company) was formed on July 20, 2011 and is owned 100% by Citizens Enterprises Corporation (Parent). The Company leases 50% of the transfer capability of the Border East Transmission line from San Diego Gas &amp;amp; Electric, which is a 30 mile portion of the 117 mile Sunrise Powerlink Transmission Project, which provides over 1,000 MW of transmission capacity connecting the San Diego metropolitan area with renewable resources in California's Imperial Valley. The transmission line is maintained by San Diego Gas &amp;amp; Electric (SDG&amp;amp;E), which CST reimburses for related costs incurred. All of CST's revenues are from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) approved Transmission Revenue Requirement (TRR) tariff and are collected by the California Independent System Operator (ISO) from users of the transmission line and remitted to the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Company.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect certain reported amounts and disclosures. Accordingly, actual results could differ from those&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;estimates.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Accounts Receivable and the Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.3pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company leases 50% of a transmission line and derives its revenue from a FERC-approved TTR tariff, which is collected by the California ISO from users and remitted monthly to the Company and due in 30 days. Accounts receivable are stated at the contractual amount billed to the customer. The Company recognized an allowance for losses on accounts receivable in an amount equal to current expected credit losses. The estimation of the allowance is based on an analysis of historical loss experience, current receivables aging, and management's assessment of current conditions and reasonable and supportable expectation of future conditions, as well as an assessment of specific identifiable customer accounts considered at risk or uncollectible. The Company assesses collectability by pooling receivables where similar characteristics exist and evaluates receivables individually when a specific customer balance no longer shares those risk characteristics and are considered a risk or uncollectible. The expense associated with the allowance for expected credit losses is included in general and administrative expenses.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.35pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has elected an accounting policy to consider subsequent collection activity in measuring expected credit losses. Accordingly, trade receivables that are collected in full after the balance sheet date, but before the date the financial statements are available to be issued are excluded from the credit loss measurement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.35pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Receivables are written off when information indicates the debtor is experiencing significant financial difficulty and recovery is no longer considered possible. Recoveries of amounts previously written off are recognized in income or as an offset to credit loss expense in the period recovered. Credit losses are expected to be minimal. Accordingly, no provision for credit losses has been included in the financial statements.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.35pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 4.6pt; margin-left: 22.75pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.5pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Revenues are derived through the TRR which is collected by the California ISO. During the years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, 100% of the Company's revenue and 100% of the accounts receivable balance at December 31, 2025 and 2024 were derived from the California&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ISO.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Fair Value of Financial Instruments&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company's financial instruments consist of cash, cash held in escrow, accounts receivable, accounts payable and accrued expenses, and debt instruments. The carrying values of cash, cash held in escrow, accounts receivable, and accounts payable and accrued expenses are generally considered to be representative of their respective fair values because of their short-term nature. The carrying values of the Company's debt instruments approximate their fair values as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, based on the incremental borrowing rates for similar types of borrowing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;arrangements.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company recognizes the provision of transmission services in accordance with the TRR as an operating lease with payments depending on the transmission facility being under the operational control of the California ISO. The Company recognizes rental revenue which is shown in the accompanying financial statements as electric revenue while the transmission facility is under the operational control of the California ISO during the term of the lease. The Company's revenue does not fall under the guidance of ASU 2014-09, Revenue from Contracts with Customers (Topic 606) because the standard explicitly excludes lease-based income.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Deferred Finance Charges&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Interest Topic of the FASB Accounting Standards Codification requires the Company to present deferred finance charges as a reduction of the carrying amount of the debt rather than as an asset (see Note 4). The costs are amortized using the interest method over the life of the debt. Amortization of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;debt issuance costs of approximately $83,000 was charged to interest expense for both of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024. Amortization of debt issuance costs for the next five years is expected to be approximately $83,000 per year.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Prepaid Operating Lease Right-of-Use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.7pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company leases 50% of the transfer capability of a transmission line located in California's Imperial Valley. On July 3, 2012, CST paid for the 30-year transmission line lease with SDG&amp;amp;E at inception of the lease agreement and is amortizing it on a straight-line basis over the term of the arrangement. The prepaid operating lease right-of-use asset (ROU) is included in current assets and other assets on the Company's balance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;sheets.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;An ROU asset represents the Company's right to use the underlying asset for the lease term. The entire lease obligation was paid in full at inception, therefore there is no recognition of a lease liability. Lease expense will be recognized on a straight-line basis over the lease term and the lease does not contain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;any renewal options. The Company does not anticipate that it will need to enter any new leases in the foreseeable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;future.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold"&gt;Regulatory Asset&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;CST is a regulated entity, and in appropriate circumstances, establishes regulatory assets or liabilities, and thereby defers the income statement impact of certain charges or revenues because it is probable to be collected or refunded through future customer billings as required by the Accounting of Certain Types of Regulation Topic of the FASB Accounting Standards Codification. During 2012, CST received regulatory approval from the FERC to capitalize development costs associated with setting up the CST transmission project. CST is amortizing these costs over the thirty-year life of the lease and are reimbursed through the TRR. The over-collections of TRR tariffs are returned to ratepayers in future rate filings and are classified as a regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;liability.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.15pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Allocation of Profits, Losses, and Member Distributions&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Profits or losses from operations of the Company, along with gains and losses from the sale, exchange, or other disposition of Company property and tax credits shall be allocated annually to the sole member in accordance with the operating agreement. Net cash flow available for distribution will be paid to the sole member after all conditions contained within the operating agreement have been satisfied.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Reclassification&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;Certain prior year balances have been reclassified to conform with the presentation in the current year.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Cash Flow Information&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company considers all highly liquid debt instruments purchased with a maturity of three months or less to be cash equivalents.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0.4pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Supplemental disclosure of cash flow information:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="margin-left: 53.05pt; border-collapse: collapse"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.1pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 270.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 104.3pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 53.7pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 10.65pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 32.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 10.65pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 25.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 270.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin: 0 102.55pt 0 52.85pt; text-indent: -21.6pt; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;Cash paid during the years for: Income taxes&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 104.3pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 57.35pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 57.35pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 20.85pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 270.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-left: 52.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Interest&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 104.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 18.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;3,573,457&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 18.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;3,698,149&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 45.2pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 270.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 7.5pt; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold"&gt;Cash and Cash Held in Escrow&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;Cash and cash held in escrow consist of the following:&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 104.3pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.45pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 53.7pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.05pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top